-- R10-GENERIC-HEAT-CURVE — the displace through a number entity, kind offset
  ok   no topic and an offset entity: one publish of 5 sends one set_value of 5 (R10-GENERIC-HEAT-CURVE)
  ok   the entity option empty: no set_value, and the /set topic still carries the integer (W7)
  ok   both configured: MQTT first with the full integer, the entity bounded by the 3 K default band
  ok   a kelvin entity is sent -2 for -2, never 271.15 through the absolute helpers (T1)
  ok   a Fahrenheit entity is sent the difference x9/5: 2 K is 3.6 °F (T1)
  ok   an entity range narrower than the displace saturates and is latched once, naming it (W6)
  ok   a reading already at the target is not written (W1)
  ok   inside the grace a differing reading proves nothing: no second write (W2)
  ok   after the grace the first miss is written once more (W2)
  ok   a second miss for the same target latches a warning and sends nothing (W3)
  ok   and a new target is written again (W3)
  ok   the 24 h write guard is 2 x 1440 / interval: 96 at the default 30 min (W4)
  ok   at the guard nothing is written and it is latched; one below it the write goes (W4)
  ok   absent, unavailable, a non-temperature unit, a sensor, a range without 0 or a raising service: no value lands, the failure is latched, the MQTT arm still publishes
  ok   MODE_OFF after a write writes one 0 (the off rule)
  ok   and while off the arm writes nothing, nor does a second off
  ok   nothing written, nothing restored; an unconfigured entity is never written
  ok   unload after a write writes one 0, through async_unload_entry (the off rule)
  ok   MODE_OFF and unload leave displace 0 standing on both ECL110 topics, retain on and off
  ok   the legacy neutral body releases supply: heat_pump_on true, displace 0, reason off_restore
  ok   publish_ecl110_topics with no topic configured publishes nothing and reports success
  ok   an MQTT arm never published is not restored; one published is restored once, not per off
  ok   a topic refusing the neutral leaves the MQTT arm armed and counts no restore
  ok   an MQTT arm whose topics were cleared is disarmed unwritten, no restore counted
  ok   the legacy payload's heat_pump_on is the switch's write, inside its step and a step late; no write and no key: off
  ok   a write left armed by a crash is restored by the next run's first off
  ok   a stand-in second consumer registers without editing the hook: its baseline, captured before its first write, survives a restart and is what the restore writes
  ok   and an unreadable baseline refuses the consumer's write: nothing to restore it to
  ok   an unregistered consumer, or one its factory reads as unconfigured, refuses the write and leaves no record behind
  ok   a restore whose write raises sends nothing, stays armed and latches a warning naming the entity
  ok   and the next off retries it: one write of the neutral 0, disarmed and counted
  ok   an armed consumer no longer configured is disarmed unwritten: its entity is not the optimizer's
  ok   a store that cannot save still arms the write, and one that cannot be removed does not raise
  ok   T2 at its bounds: a range starting or ending at 0 is an offset, one starting at 0.5 or ending at -0.5 is not
  ok   every refusal of the pure convert names why and is never read as saturated
  ok   a range narrower than the displace saturates on the low side too: -3 K sends -2 (W6)
  ok   a reading exactly half a step from the target holds: 2.25 against 2 at step 0.5 is not written (W1)
  ok   a target within half a step of the last write is that write, still in its grace: 3 after 2 at step 2 sends nothing (W2)
  ok   a reading that held clears the misses, and the grace is 90 s: a miss 91 s after the write is written once more, not given up (W1, W2)
  ok   writes older than 24 h leave the guard: a full day of them 24 h and 1 s old blocks nothing (W4)
  ok   at exactly 90 s the grace is over: a miss then is written once more (W2's bound)
  ok   and a write exactly 24 h old still counts: a full day of them at that age blocks the write (W4's bound)
  ok   the entity arm answers True only for a write sent: held, capped and unreadable are False
  ok   a write that succeeds clears the failure latch, and so does a readable entity: the next failure is warned again, not swallowed
  ok   the heat-curve diagnostics: zeros before any write, the write and its 24 h count after one
  ok   publish called without mode_off writes the entity: only the off mode suppresses the arm
  ok   a restore that succeeded cleared its latch: the next failed restore is warned again
  ok   and after the retry succeeds no failure is held for that consumer
  ok   a write the restore hook refuses to arm is never sent: the arm refuses before the write
  ok   a heat-curve write armed before its entity option was cleared is disarmed unwritten at the next off
  ok   a mode change that is not into off, or off to off, restores nothing and answers 0
  ok   a restore is persisted, so the next run does not restore it again; a forgotten entry's armed set is gone from the store
  ok   the persisted armed set is read once per entry, not at every arm
  ok   the off-restore store is at version 1: a bump strands every persisted armed set without a migration
  ok   a factory reset keeps the heat-curve kind beside its entity (ghc-d03)
  ok   off then on inside the grace, plan unchanged: the re-enable rewrites 2 over the restore's 0, never held as W2's grace of the write before the off
  ok   a rewrite that held, then off and on at the same target: 2 is written again and W3 does not latch against the restore's own 0
  ok   null control, the same history without the off and on: the held 2 is not rewritten, nothing warned
  ok   unload, then the reloaded coordinator for the same entry inside the grace: 2 is written over the restore's 0
  ok   a re-enable at 0 right after a restore that did not hold is inside the restore's own grace (W2)
  ok   and after its grace the restore's first miss is written once more, not given up on the plan's earlier miss (W3)
  ok   a restore whose write raised leaves the arm's record at the plan's write
  ok   the peak guard's engage writes the plan less the nudge to the entity, its release the plan again
  ok   boost writes the displace maximum to the entity, the boost mode and the space boost overlay alike
  ok   the learned curve bias reaches the entity: 3 with a -1 bias sends 2; with curve learning off, 3
  ok   the chokepoint called while off writes no entity value; the MQTT arm still carries the integer

-- R10-GENERIC-HEAT-CURVE-PERSISTENT — kind persistent: a stored curve parameter
  ok   kind persistent: displace 2 on a 22 °C parameter writes 24 and records {number.x, 22} before it
  ok   kind persistent's defaults are the research's: a 3 K band, 12 writes a day, a 60 min dwell (O5)
  ok   the band bounds the displace: 8 K on a 22 °C baseline writes 25, never 30 (I1)
  ok   a Fahrenheit parameter is displaced by whole steps inside the band: 2 K is 3.6 °F, sent as 3.5 (I1)
  ok   the entity's own range bounds it too: max 23 sends 23
  ok   a reading that holds the last write is ours, never an edit: the baseline is not re-saved
  ok   a reading already at the target is not written, armed or not (W1)
  ok   the dwell holds a second change for 60 min after the last write, and releases it after (P5)
  ok   budget 2: one displace and its restore; a second displace, or a return to the baseline the restore would repeat, is refused, so the day's writes never pass the budget (P4, I2)
  ok   budget 0, and budget 1 whose one write is the one kept back, write nothing, so nothing is armed and nothing restored, as the docs say (fix review 1 of #3402). Null control: budget 2 writes 24 above
  ok   a new local day starts the count afresh: yesterday's full budget blocks nothing, today's one write does
