-- R10-DUTY-SWITCH-PLANNER-PRICE: the planner prices a duty switch that stops the compressor (pull request 3420, Bankaifan)
  ok   a hot-water step into a heating step at equal draw costs the start term nothing at the boundary and weighs p x draw / p_max as a switch
  ok   the stop adds the smaller of the two levels across a boundary
  ok   an idle step between the two duties is no switch
  ok   the reverse order is the other direction: unpriced with a zero there, priced by its own probability
  ok   a two-leg both step alone weighs p x (space + dhw) / p_max: both legs run at the step's combined level
  ok   a both step followed by heating is one switch, not two: its last leg is already heating
  ok   null control: a zero pair weighs every one of those plans zero
  ok   the relaxed descent's term is cycling_cost x that weight and the true objective's cycling_cost x the probability of one start, a float for one plan and one entry per row for a batch; the unpriced descent has none
  ok   and it is no operand at all with a zero pair, a zero cycling cost or no hot-water plan
  ok   a non-finite, negative, over-one or misshapen learned pair reads as zero
  ok   the leaf's legs are what step_duty and _share serve over the probe grid, floor unset and set: idle, one duty, both collapse edges and two legs
  ok   and the grid holds what it claims: two-leg cells under both floors, fewer with the floor set, and both exact collapse edges (shares of 5 and 10 minutes)
  ok   the same agreement on the levels a clamped install ships: a modulating pump keeps two-leg steps, each circuit at or above p_min
  ok   and on a fixed-speed pump the leaf never returns two legs, while the row still holds heating-only and hot-water-only steps
  ok   switch_weights_batch is switch_weight on every row, bit for bit, floor unset and set
  ok   a pump with no maximum draw weighs every row zero, one finite entry per row and not per step, on the rows the priced pair weighs above
  ok   a block end charges one step, the one holding the heating leg that follows it: the step after the block when heating starts there, not the block's last
  ok   the block's own last step when it is a two-leg step, and then not the step after
  ok   no vector at all with a zero lost share, with an idle step after the block, or with no hot water: the caller makes today's calls
